## Why This Is Asked
Tests structuring a dynamic, duplicate-friendly grouping based on a stable signature.

## Key Concepts
- Canonical form via sorted letters for anagram grouping
- Nested maps to track per-word counts within a signature bucket
- Amortized update and linear-time retrieval relative to output size

## Code Example
```javascript
class AnagramMultiset {
  constructor(){ this.sigMap = new Map(); }
  _sig(w){ return w.split('').sort().join(''); }
  insert(word){ const s = this._sig(word); const bucket = this.sigMap.get(s) || new Map(); bucket.set(word, (bucket.get(word) || 0) + 1); this.sigMap.set(s, bucket); }
  erase(word){ const s = this._sig(word); const bucket = this.sigMap.get(s); if(!bucket) return; const c = (bucket.get(word) || 0) - 1; if(c<=0){ bucket.delete(word); if(bucket.size===0) this.sigMap.delete(s);} else { bucket.set(word, c); } }
  getAnagrams(word){ const s = this._sig(word); const bucket = this.sigMap.get(s); if(!bucket) return []; const res = []; for(const [w,c] of bucket) for(let i=0;i<c;i++) res.push(w); return res; }
}
```

